      "Forward, reverse, junction-capacitance, and power-derating curves were digitized from the plotted vector paths on p. 2; no points were extrapolated beyond the plotted ranges.",
      "Fig. 1 contains Ta = 100 degC and Ta = 25 degC forward-current curves with VF plotted from 0 to 600 mV and IF plotted logarithmically from 0.01 to 100 mA.",
      "Fig. 2 contains Ta = 100 degC and Ta = 25 degC reverse-current curves with VR plotted from 0 to 40 V and IR plotted logarithmically from 0.01 to 100 nA.",
      "Fig. 3 is a typical CT versus VR curve at Ta = 25 degC and f = 1 MHz; the table separately gives CT typ. 2 pF at VR = 1 V.",
      "Fig. 4 is a power derating curve plotted through Ta = 125 degC; no value beyond the plotted endpoint was added.",
      "Maximum ratings on p. 1 include VRRM = 40 V, IF(AV) = 0.03 A, Tj = 125 degC, PD = 200 mW, and R_thetaJA = 500 degC/W; the schema has no dedicated fields for these ratings.",
      "The datasheet publishes no reverse-recovery-time or breakdown-characteristic value, so reverse_recovery, breakdown_voltage, and breakdown_current are null."
